**New evidence**
- Marcos framed the China relationship as something broader than the South China Sea dispute and said he would seek ways to resolve conflicts and normalize ties.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Marcos: PHL, China should not only talk about sea disputes","publisher":"BusinessWorld Online","publication_date":"2022-07-05","url":"https://www.bworldonline.com/the-nation/2022/07/05/459321/marcos-phl-china-should-not-only-talk-about-sea-disputes/","claim":"Marcos said the Philippines and China should explore cooperation beyond territorial disputes, and that he would meet Wang Yi to find ways to resolve conflicts and normalize relations.","locator":"lines 87-96","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous local reporting with direct quotations from Marcos.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 ruler-period evidence, before the November summit sequence.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Marcos’s public diplomatic stance.","contrary_evidence":["This is rhetoric and agenda-setting, not proof of durable de-escalation.","Maritime tensions with China remained unresolved."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.3","2B.7","2B.10"]}

- Ahead of ASEAN, Marcos said he would raise maritime security, the South China Sea, Myanmar, and Russia-Ukraine as regional issues for collective action.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"PBBM to raise regional cooperation in maritime, food security in ASEAN Summit","publisher":"Presidential Communications Office","publication_date":"2022-11-09","url":"https://pco.gov.ph/news_releases/pbbm-to-raise-regional-cooperation-in-maritime-food-security-in-asean-summit/","claim":"Marcos said his ASEAN participation would emphasize regional cooperation on maritime security and would address the South China Sea, Myanmar, and the Russia-Ukraine conflict.","locator":"departure statement excerpt in the Nov. 9 news release","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official presidential communications release with Marcos’s own departure remarks.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 ruler-period evidence immediately before the ASEAN summits.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Marcos’s own stated agenda.","contrary_evidence":["This is a stated agenda, not an outcome.","It does not by itself prove successful peace-building."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}

- Marcos explicitly urged a South China Sea code of conduct grounded in international law and framed it as a model for managing disputes.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"PBBM backs early conclusion of COC in South China Sea","publisher":"Presidential Communications Office","publication_date":"2022-11-11","url":"https://pco.gov.ph/news_releases/pbbm-backs-early-conclusion-of-coc-in-south-china-sea/","claim":"Marcos urged early conclusion of a South China Sea Code of Conduct based on international law and said it should show how states manage differences through reason and right.","locator":"headline and opening paragraph in the Nov. 11 news release","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official release quoting a clear Marcos intervention at the ASEAN-China Summit.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 ruler-period evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Marcos at a multilateral summit.","contrary_evidence":["A proposed code is not the same as a completed settlement.","The dispute itself continued after the speech."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}

- Marcos and Biden discussed South China Sea tensions, and Marcos emphasized the U.S. role in peace and stability in the Indo-Pacific.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Biden holds his first meeting with Philippine leader Marcos","publisher":"The Associated Press via CityNews Toronto","publication_date":"2022-09-22","url":"https://toronto.citynews.ca/2022/09/22/biden-holds-his-first-meeting-with-philippine-leader-marcos/","claim":"Biden and Marcos discussed South China Sea tensions, the U.S.-Philippines security relationship, and Marcos said the United States’ role in maintaining peace in the region was appreciated.","locator":"lines 99-108","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent contemporaneous wire reporting with direct meeting coverage.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 ruler-period evidence at the first Biden-Marcos meeting.","ruler_attribution":"Directly about Marcos’s foreign-policy posture in office.","contrary_evidence":["The meeting also reflected heightened U.S.-China tensions, so the setting was not low-pressure.","This does not show a specific Marcos de-escalation success."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.6","2B.10"]}

- Marcos publicly said the Russia-Ukraine war should stop and that the South China Sea should be a sea of peace, not armed conflict.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"40th and 41st ASEAN Summits – News Releases","publisher":"Presidential Communications Office","publication_date":"2022-11-13","url":"https://pco.gov.ph/40th-and-41st-asean-summits/news-releases/","claim":"Marcos said the Russia-Ukraine conflict should stop and all stakeholders must resort to diplomacy, and he renewed his call to make the South China Sea a sea of peace and stability rather than armed conflict.","locator":"Nov. 13 entries for the Russia-Ukraine and South China Sea news releases","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official presidential news-release page with direct Marcos quotations from the ASEAN summit period.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 ruler-period evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Marcos’s summit messaging.","contrary_evidence":["This is diplomatic messaging, not verified conflict resolution.","Regional tensions in the South China Sea persisted."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}

- Marcos described his meeting with Xi as a pleasant exchange centered on regional issues and the upcoming state visit.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"PBBM elated over Xi meeting; looks forward to China state visit","publisher":"Presidential Communications Office","publication_date":"2022-11-17","url":"https://pco.gov.ph/news_releases/pbbm-elated-over-xi-meeting-looks-forward-to-china-state-visit/","claim":"After meeting Xi Jinping in Bangkok, Marcos said the encounter was a pleasant exchange and that they mostly discussed regional issues and his planned state visit to China.","locator":"news release body and quoted remarks","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official presidential release immediately after the bilateral meeting.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 ruler-period evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Marcos’s bilateral diplomacy.","contrary_evidence":["Tone is not outcome; it does not show a concrete settlement.","The South China Sea dispute remained unresolved after the meeting."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}

- Marcos ordered a diplomatic note to China after the Pag-asa debris incident, using clarification rather than force.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Philippines sends note verbale to China over Pag-asa incident","publisher":"GMA News Online","publication_date":"2022-11-24","url":"https://www.gmanetwork.com/news/topstories/nation/852456/philippines-sends-note-verbale-to-china-over-pag-asa-incident/story/","claim":"The DFA said a note verbale was sent following the President’s instruction to seek clarification from China over the Pag-asa incident.","locator":"lines 114-147","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous local report with direct attribution to Marcos’s instruction and DFA action.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 ruler-period evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Marcos through the reported instruction to send the note.","contrary_evidence":["The same article shows the episode was disputed and not fully resolved.","A note verbale is a diplomatic response, not a demonstrated long-term settlement."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.6","2B.9","2B.10"]}

- Reuters reporting captured Marcos saying the Philippines would issue a diplomatic note because the Chinese and Philippine accounts differed, reinforcing a procedural, not military, response.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Philippines to send diplomatic note to Beijing on South China Sea incident","publisher":"Reuters via ThePrint","publication_date":"2022-11-22","url":"https://theprint.in/world/philippines-to-send-diplomatic-note-to-beijing-on-south-china-sea-incident/1229491/","claim":"Marcos said the Philippines would issue a diplomatic note to Beijing after a South China Sea debris incident because the Chinese account differed from the Philippine Navy’s report.","locator":"Reuters passage beginning with Marcos’s comment on the differing accounts","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire report syndicated on a host site; useful independent corroboration of the president’s response.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 ruler-period evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Directly about Marcos’s reaction to the incident.","contrary_evidence":["The article shows a real maritime dispute, so the environment was not calm.","The response remains diplomatic rather than a proven de-escalatory outcome."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.6","2B.9","2B.10"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
I screened roughly 30 documents across official Philippine releases, Reuters republishings, AP, BusinessWorld, GMA, PNA, and several follow-up or retrospective items. I kept only sources that added something materially distinct about Marcos’s 2022 peace/security behavior.

Removed or deprioritized items fell into these buckets:
- Duplicate coverage: multiple PCO, PNA, and republished Reuters items repeated the same South China Sea, ASEAN, or China dialogue claims.
- Out of period: 2023 state-visit materials, 2024 bilateral-defense updates, and 2026 anniversary statements were informative but not 2022 evidence.
- Weak or irrelevant: climate-only, general economy, or nuclear-energy-only items did not add 2B value beyond the diplomacy and maritime-dispute material already retained.
- Blocked or unstable fetches: some PCO pages returned internal errors or cache misses when opened directly, so I used accessible official pages or reliable republications instead.
- Domestic-only material: internal repression, policing, and rights reporting were excluded unless they directly touched foreign-policy or alliance conduct.

**Remaining gaps**
- There is still no evidence that Marcos initiated an interstate war, used force offensively, or prolonged a war of choice in 2022. The structured prior and the narrative record both point to a limited-exposure case.
- I did not find strong evidence for 2B.8 beyond ordinary defense modernization and alliance management. There is no clear record of military spending being used to intimidate neighbors or reward security elites.
- I did not find a ruler-specific 2B.9 accountability episode beyond the Pag-asa note-verbale response. That supports clarification and protest, but not a deeper accountability record.
- More search could refine the maritime-incident timeline and the defense-modernization side, but it is unlikely to change the core picture: Marcos’s 2022 international-security conduct was diplomacy-heavy, not war-driven.
